  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final rules adopt a 55°C test with a 5% failure-rate threshold, but above-limit sales are not barred—only corrective action and retesting within 12 months. Per-model failure rates go to customers and regulators, but not the public. S3 requires remote shut-off on new units within 36 months but sets no retrofit deadline for installed units. S4 mandates built-in suppression at 36 months. S5 mandates recall at 8 incidents/100k with prompt notice, but lacks a serious-injury clause."
